WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:02:16.159 --> 00:02:22.039
I left China in 2011.


00:02:22.331 --> 00:02:25.709
I left to find something I'd
been searching for all my life.


00:02:28.668 --> 00:02:31.796
Along the way, I've learned
I'm not the only one looking.


00:02:45.725 --> 00:02:48.728
Traveling was one of the few
freedoms I knew in China.


00:02:51.897 --> 00:02:54.315
Every year since I
was 20 years old,


00:02:54.607 --> 00:03:00.070
I would celebrate my birthday
by traveling to a new place.


00:03:00.362 --> 00:03:02.655
I started this
tradition in China.


00:03:02.947 --> 00:03:05.075
On my first birthday
living in New York,


00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:08.243
I bought a one-way ticket
and went to Florida.


00:03:12.831 --> 00:03:15.792
I was excited to document
every conversation I had.


00:03:16.084 --> 00:03:17.210
Welcome to America.


00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:19.711
Like this is-- this is
what America is like.


00:03:20.003 --> 00:03:22.798
Since I was a teen, I just
wanted to grab a backpack


00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:24.632
and go travel, you
know, not knowing


00:03:24.924 --> 00:03:26.926
where I'm going to sleep or
who I'm going to be with.


00:03:27.218 --> 00:03:28.427
That excited me.


00:03:28.719 --> 00:03:30.846
Tell me what's
your next plan-- travel?


00:03:31.138 --> 00:03:33.723
I'm going to South
America for six months.


00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:40.521
A few days into
the trip, I stayed at a hostel


00:03:40.813 --> 00:03:42.730
where I met someone
whose mode of travel


00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.399
was different from
anyone I knew.


00:04:10.379 --> 00:04:11.379
How do you spell your name?


00:04:19.136 --> 00:04:20.011
Dylan.


00:04:20.303 --> 00:04:21.054
Dylan.


00:04:21.346 --> 00:04:22.139
And your last name?


00:04:22.431 --> 00:04:24.057
Olsen.


00:04:26.809 --> 00:04:28.394
The first
night I met Dylan,


00:04:28.686 --> 00:04:32.605
we talked for hours about
our lives and travels.


00:04:32.897 --> 00:04:35.441
What did you have when
you first got on the road?


00:04:35.732 --> 00:04:38.569
An empty backpack
and no money.


00:04:38.861 --> 00:04:41.738
I just began to travel
across the country.


00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:45.825
How can you pay the
hostel if you don't have money?


00:04:46.117 --> 00:04:48.536
I-- I worked for them.


00:04:48.828 --> 00:04:54.416
I-- I came here offering
my work for a place


00:04:54.708 --> 00:05:00.170
to close my eyes at night that
was safe and a place to just


00:05:00.462 --> 00:05:02.630
to be at peace.


00:05:22.771 --> 00:05:23.939
So many
people come and go,


00:05:24.231 --> 00:05:25.232
it's hard to remember.


00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:27.026
I do know that when
I first met Dylan,


00:05:27.318 --> 00:05:29.653
I immediately identified
he was a street kid.


00:05:29.945 --> 00:05:31.446
How?


00:05:31.738 --> 00:05:34.657
Just because
he's a street kid.


00:05:34.949 --> 00:05:37.744
You meet so many people,
you can see certain things.


00:05:38.035 --> 00:05:39.411
It's evident.


00:05:39.703 --> 00:05:42.789
And so we had a conversation
and made the agreement


00:05:43.081 --> 00:05:48.460
that he would leave all those
survival skills of the street


00:05:48.752 --> 00:05:49.920
behind.


00:05:50.212 --> 00:05:52.881
They have no place here.


00:05:53.173 --> 00:05:55.674
We identified that immediately.


00:05:55.966 --> 00:05:58.135
And it's very rare
that we'll allow that.


00:05:58.427 --> 00:06:02.680
But he's unique-- very
smart, very creative.


00:06:02.972 --> 00:06:06.434
He's got one of the best
skills that you can have--


00:06:06.726 --> 00:06:09.894
fearless in working--
fearless in doing.


00:07:20.121 --> 00:07:21.746
- I
- wanted to experience the life


00:07:22.038 --> 00:07:24.331
that Dylan described to me.


00:07:24.623 --> 00:07:26.083
When he went back
to the streets,


00:07:26.375 --> 00:07:29.919
I decided to follow him with
my camera despite the fact


00:07:30.211 --> 00:07:32.130
that I hardly knew him.


00:07:52.646 --> 00:07:54.398
Oh, we need a better map.


00:08:02.572 --> 00:08:04.073
Being
lost is where I'm found.


00:08:08.077 --> 00:08:11.621
Upon arriving the path
that I am happy to tread,


00:08:11.912 --> 00:08:15.666
my shoes come off, and I
experience that full connection


00:08:15.958 --> 00:08:16.791
with the floor.


00:08:17.083 --> 00:08:19.919
It's as if I can breathe better.


00:08:20.211 --> 00:08:23.548
Observing everybody else
around in their entirety,


00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:27.718
their passions, their
bizarre behaviors,


00:08:28.010 --> 00:08:31.430
as well as their observing
me and my bizarre behaviors.


00:08:48.568 --> 00:08:51.821
There's no time
living in this sense.


00:08:52.113 --> 00:08:54.324
I don't know what day it is.


00:08:54.616 --> 00:08:56.825
Every day is now, right now.


00:08:57.117 --> 00:08:57.993
Every time is right now.


00:09:04.331 --> 00:09:05.457
I taught Dylan


00:09:05.749 --> 00:09:07.959
how to use my camera
so he could document


00:09:08.251 --> 00:09:09.211
my experiences a while.


00:09:16.801 --> 00:09:22.013
This was the first time I ate
food from our garbage can.


00:09:22.305 --> 00:09:24.599
It was the beginning of
my short street life.


00:09:40.737 --> 00:09:42.489
"Wherever
he goes, he leaves an echo


00:09:42.781 --> 00:09:45.866
to show from the pitter
patter of his feet


00:09:46.158 --> 00:09:49.245
to the magic incantation
he speaks, a man


00:09:49.536 --> 00:09:52.496
from the past living
in the present.


00:09:52.788 --> 00:09:55.791
So his presence is
living in the future.


00:09:56.083 --> 00:09:59.627
Yesterday and tomorrow-- last
week was seven years long."


00:11:18.693 --> 00:11:20.195
Why you choose
to be on the street?


00:11:20.487 --> 00:11:21.696
Hmm.


00:11:21.988 --> 00:11:23.490
Why are you choosing
to stay on the street?


00:11:27.825 --> 00:11:28.576
Well--


00:11:28.868 --> 00:11:29.869
Huh?


00:11:30.161 --> 00:11:34.414
I guess the only
objective is eating,


00:11:34.706 --> 00:11:38.710
and happiness, and community.


00:11:39.002 --> 00:11:42.171
What do you mean eating?


00:11:42.463 --> 00:11:50.595
And I feed myself,
and I have a good attitude,


00:11:50.887 --> 00:11:52.763
and I just go
wherever I want to go.


00:11:53.055 --> 00:11:55.390
You can wander around
and see so many things


00:11:55.682 --> 00:11:57.934
and meet so many people
that none of that


00:11:58.226 --> 00:11:59.977
could ever occur if I were--


00:12:00.269 --> 00:12:05.483
if I were just staying in one
place, working for one person.


00:12:05.774 --> 00:12:08.860
I've gone through quite a
big portion of North America.


00:12:09.152 --> 00:12:12.531
I'm just exploring,
just meeting people.


00:12:12.823 --> 00:12:13.490
Hey, man, you got a Sharpie.


00:12:17.909 --> 00:12:19.369
I really couldn't
answer and say when


00:12:19.661 --> 00:12:24.248
I'll be done traveling or living
on the street in this way.


00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:27.042
But anywhere I am, something
likely amazing happens.


00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:32.797
My name is Jared.


00:12:33.089 --> 00:12:34.006
Jared.


00:12:34.298 --> 00:12:37.634
And this is my
buddy here Jong.


00:12:37.926 --> 00:12:39.219
My name is Dylan.


00:12:39.511 --> 00:12:40.220
Dylan.
Nice to meet you.


00:12:40.512 --> 00:12:41.178
Nice to meet you, man.


00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:43.138
My name NANFU.


00:12:44.765 --> 00:12:46.307
That's cool.


00:12:46.599 --> 00:12:47.892
So you're from Utah, you said?
- Yeah.


00:12:48.184 --> 00:12:48.810
Originally?


00:12:49.102 --> 00:12:49.853
Yeah.


00:12:50.144 --> 00:12:50.895
What part did you say?


00:12:51.187 --> 00:12:52.480
Just north of Salt Lake City.


00:12:52.772 --> 00:12:53.856
Did you grow up Mormon?


00:12:54.147 --> 00:12:58.193
Uh, yeah, for a minute.


00:12:58.485 --> 00:12:59.069
For a hot minute?


00:12:59.361 --> 00:13:00.904
Yeah, for a hot minute.


00:13:01.195 --> 00:13:02.280
You are welcome
to stay the night.


00:13:02.572 --> 00:13:03.197
Neat.


00:13:03.489 --> 00:13:04.782
That's a pullout.


00:13:05.074 --> 00:13:11.203
She needs a good rest,
so she's earned it.


00:13:11.495 --> 00:13:13.414
One of the first people
to buy here in the 1960s.


00:13:13.706 --> 00:13:14.498
Jared had


00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:15.958
known us for just a few hours.


00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:17.375
You guys want a beer?


00:13:17.667 --> 00:13:19.544
But he invited us home.


00:13:19.836 --> 00:13:22.797
It had been days since
I slept under a roof.


00:13:23.089 --> 00:13:24.132
So I've been there.


00:13:24.424 --> 00:13:25.966
You know, I've been
traveling by myself.


00:13:26.258 --> 00:13:27.175
I've had no place to stay.


00:13:27.467 --> 00:13:28.677
So I just figured
I'd extend a hand.


00:13:28.969 --> 00:13:31.345
And I like him, you know?


00:13:31.637 --> 00:13:32.846
He's a funny cat, man.


00:13:33.138 --> 00:13:36.057
You know, he's young,
and he's finding himself.


00:13:36.349 --> 00:13:40.103
It's tough living life on
the street and on the roads.


00:13:40.395 --> 00:13:42.938
Jared
took us to dinner that night.


00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:47.151
I told myself one day I'd
come back and thank him.


00:13:47.443 --> 00:13:49.027
But I don't even
remember where he lived.


00:13:52.113 --> 00:13:53.448
Am in the camera?


00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:55.949
Yeah.


00:13:56.241 --> 00:13:57.533
- A beer, right?
- A Budweiser, please.


00:13:57.825 --> 00:13:58.868
- Budweiser.
- Thank you.


00:14:05.707 --> 00:14:06.541
Oh, OK.


00:14:39.361 --> 00:14:40.195
Oh, OK.


00:14:45.657 --> 00:14:48.451
Oh, yeah, yeah.


00:14:48.743 --> 00:14:50.244
I hadn't told my family


00:14:50.536 --> 00:14:53.121
that I was living on the
streets with someone I just


00:14:53.413 --> 00:14:57.000
met and wasn't involved with.


00:14:57.292 --> 00:14:59.419
They wouldn't understand
why a homeless person


00:14:59.711 --> 00:15:01.420
would be worth following.


00:15:01.712 --> 00:15:04.590
The idea that someone
would choose to be homeless


00:15:04.882 --> 00:15:06.801
would be inconceivable to them.


00:15:07.093 --> 00:15:10.928
But this was a kind of freedom
I had never encountered before.


00:15:18.226 --> 00:15:21.312
Everywhere we went, I was
amazed by how many people


00:15:21.604 --> 00:15:23.106
were interested in this life.


00:15:23.398 --> 00:15:24.231
- Don or Dylan?
- Dylan.


00:15:24.523 --> 00:15:25.691
Dylan.


00:15:25.983 --> 00:15:28.151
How long are you
planning to do this?


00:15:28.443 --> 00:15:29.194
I don't know, man.


00:15:29.486 --> 00:15:31.487
I have no idea.


00:15:31.779 --> 00:15:33.738
I'll see where
the road takes me.


00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.115
I'm just fascinated.


00:15:35.407 --> 00:15:37.033
So what made you like--
did someone else do


00:15:37.325 --> 00:15:39.202
this that you decided to do it?


00:15:39.493 --> 00:15:40.869
I wondered


00:15:41.161 --> 00:15:44.665
if the presence of my camera
affected how people behave.


00:15:44.957 --> 00:15:47.251
So sometimes I would
retreat from Dylan


00:15:47.542 --> 00:15:48.876
and wait until
something happened.


00:15:51.629 --> 00:15:54.590
This guy met Dylan in
front of a coffee shop


00:15:54.882 --> 00:15:58.259
while I was sitting inside
charging my battery.


00:15:58.551 --> 00:15:59.969
They talked for hours.


00:16:00.261 --> 00:16:02.221
And then he invited
Dylan to his home.


00:16:02.513 --> 00:16:04.305
We were just carrying
a conversation,


00:16:04.597 --> 00:16:06.266
and we got something in
common with a hostile.


00:16:06.558 --> 00:16:09.644
I stayed in a hostile
that was in California.


00:16:09.936 --> 00:16:13.147
I just decided that it was good
to have some money to give.


00:16:13.439 --> 00:16:15.983
It just makes me feel
good to be able to--


00:16:16.275 --> 00:16:18.943
makes me feel good it
you can help somebody.


00:16:19.235 --> 00:16:22.362
What part of
his story interested you?


00:16:22.654 --> 00:16:24.865
Well, I guess the way--


00:16:25.157 --> 00:16:27.742
the choices he makes.


00:16:28.034 --> 00:16:29.618
Street life was


00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:33.164
free and exciting for Dylan.


00:16:33.456 --> 00:16:35.248
But it wasn't that
way for everyone.


00:16:40.336 --> 00:16:43.422
Why were people so generous to
Dylan, but not to the others?


00:16:47.383 --> 00:16:49.844
I began to realize the
privilege of choosing


00:16:50.136 --> 00:16:53.138
to be on the streets,
which includes both of us.


00:17:54.189 --> 00:17:55.982
A little
something to get people here.


00:17:56.274 --> 00:17:58.485
Who came here a member?


00:17:59.944 --> 00:18:01.986
Who
came-- did anybody


00:18:02.278 --> 00:18:03.988
come to meet with God tonight?


00:18:07.325 --> 00:18:09.452
Well, we're glad that you
chose to come here tonight.


00:18:09.743 --> 00:18:11.203
Who has been here
before and decided


00:18:11.495 --> 00:18:12.955
they might come back again?


00:18:14.748 --> 00:18:16.375
All right, well, I think
we're in the right place.


00:18:16.667 --> 00:18:17.708
So let's pray over the meal.


00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.502
Father, I thank you for tonight.


00:18:19.794 --> 00:18:20.670
I think you--


00:18:20.962 --> 00:18:21.546
I just love--


00:18:21.838 --> 00:18:22.964
I love humanity.


00:18:23.256 --> 00:18:25.257
I'm here experiencing
humanity at its most.


00:18:25.548 --> 00:18:30.094
Do you have like any
type of like legal issues


00:18:30.386 --> 00:18:32.012
in your background that--


00:18:32.304 --> 00:18:34.055
that would, you know, add--


00:18:34.347 --> 00:18:35.056
I'm just curious, to like--


00:18:35.348 --> 00:18:36.349
Nothing extreme.


00:18:36.641 --> 00:18:39.644
I mean, I made a
lot of mistakes.


00:18:39.936 --> 00:18:41.979
By the time I was 14, I
was on heroin and selling


00:18:42.271 --> 00:18:44.648
drugs till about 20 years old.


00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:46.567
I mean, I'm
assuming you probably


00:18:46.859 --> 00:18:47.943
have maybe some
high school or you


00:18:48.234 --> 00:18:49.442
may have finished high school?


00:18:49.734 --> 00:18:50.902
I finished high
school-- did some college.


00:18:51.194 --> 00:18:51.987
OK.


00:18:52.279 --> 00:18:54.364
I quit college,
because I mean,


00:18:54.656 --> 00:18:56.825
I can learn more in a library
than I could at a school,


00:18:57.117 --> 00:18:58.909
studying what I'm
interested in for free.


00:18:59.201 --> 00:19:00.661
The point I'm
trying to bring out


00:19:00.953 --> 00:19:05.874
is that it's going to be that
much harder for you basically


00:19:06.166 --> 00:19:09.711
putting this on your resume
when you're trying to get a job.


00:19:10.003 --> 00:19:11.588
I mean, I'm having a
hard enough time myself.


00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.421
I don't feel as
if I'm doing wrong.


00:19:13.713 --> 00:19:15.798
Maybe I'm doing different
than anybody else would think.


00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:16.883
But man-- I'm--


00:19:17.175 --> 00:19:18.134
No, it's not that.


00:19:18.426 --> 00:19:19.635
I'm whole.


00:19:19.927 --> 00:19:20.678
Right, no, I'm not
saying you're doing wrong.


00:19:20.969 --> 00:19:22.012
I know that.
I know.


00:19:22.304 --> 00:19:23.430
But yeah, no, I'm
just saying, you know--


00:19:23.722 --> 00:19:25.098
I'm just telling how
I-- how I feel about it.


00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:28.934
You know, it just-- it just
seems like, you know, like--


00:19:29.226 --> 00:19:30.811
the easier way out.


00:19:31.103 --> 00:19:32.605
For now, I'm only 22.


00:19:32.897 --> 00:19:35.149
Fuck, I feel like a


00:19:35.441 --> 00:19:37.108
100-year-old person.


00:19:37.399 --> 00:19:40.777
I mean, I've been through a
lot, I've lived through a lot,


00:19:41.069 --> 00:19:43.739
and experienced a lot of
beautiful and ugly places.


00:19:44.031 --> 00:19:45.198
Dylan told me later


00:19:45.489 --> 00:19:47.241
that he was angry
for the condescension


00:19:47.533 --> 00:19:49.452
he felt from this person.


00:19:49.744 --> 00:19:52.913
He told me how much he resented
the judgment religious people


00:19:53.205 --> 00:19:55.999
had shown him in his life.


00:19:56.291 --> 00:19:58.376
But I was amazed by
how comfortable he


00:19:58.668 --> 00:20:01.462
seemed in situations like this.


00:20:01.753 --> 00:20:03.463
Hallelujah, holy,


00:20:03.755 --> 00:20:08.550
holy, God almighty, great I am.


00:20:08.842 --> 00:20:09.426
I'm so sorry.


00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:15.766
This is Dylan.


00:20:16.058 --> 00:20:17.016
Hi, Dylan, welcome.


00:20:17.308 --> 00:20:17.892
God bless you.


00:20:18.184 --> 00:20:19.143
And who is your friend?


00:20:19.435 --> 00:20:20.811
This is NANFU.


00:20:21.103 --> 00:20:22.313
Hi.


00:20:22.605 --> 00:20:23.564
- Hi, NANFU.
- And what are you doing?


00:20:23.856 --> 00:20:24.773
Just taking some shots.


00:20:25.065 --> 00:20:26.607
Filming
yeah, him, yeah.


00:20:26.899 --> 00:20:27.691
Oh, is he-- is he--


00:20:27.983 --> 00:20:28.609
Our journey.


00:20:28.901 --> 00:20:29.652
It's a journey.


00:20:29.944 --> 00:20:30.945
Oh, thank you for coming today.


00:20:31.237 --> 00:20:32.237
Fantastic!


00:20:32.528 --> 00:20:33.529
Come on in.


00:20:33.821 --> 00:20:35.990
Well, look who's back in town.


00:20:36.282 --> 00:20:38.993
They don't want to
filmed-- those two.


